No matter how long you play nethack, it seems to me there are always a few 
surprises in store. Here's one that I found this morning.

My monk went downstairs to find he was in the bigroom level with lots of 
monsters heading his way, so being a timid chap he read a scroll of earth, 
pushed out a corner, nipped round the block and back into the middle 
leaving the map looking something like this (with @ on the stairs up):

..........
...'......
....'''...
.'..'@'..^
....''....
.....'....

I've omitted the other creatures, but by now there's a big crowd formed to 
watch the entertainment. Note the extra boulder, and the related trap. The 
crowd is jostling for position, and they keep stepping onto that trap 
square.

I really didn't know you could do 'Newton's balls' in Nethack. That boulder 
is swinging back and forth more than once per turn. What fun! (The monk is 
retreating upstairs to get his health back --- the boulder keeps missing, 
but some of the creatures don't.)

